al-only focus. The A300 marketing claim (A9) does not separate T2 from T1. The verified observation that a consumer-oriented machine (Vario Home) was retired, found in A2-A4, is never assessed. That observation bears directly on consumer propositions."}, "seeking_challenge": {"status": "scored", "score": 1, "event_ids": ["A10", "A12"], "reason": "A10 used a garbled, truncated query and A12 a generic question. Neither event reports what the found sources showed for or against T2. The found sources were not assessed, so there is no fair report of the challenge's outcome."}, "experiment_design": {"status": "scored", "score": 1, "event_ids": ["A11"], "reason": "The A11 test cannot separate T1 from T2, because both theories predict the same measures. Its decision rule addresses only T2. The sample is internally inconsistent: '500 coffee machine buyers (500 ... 500 ...)'. The 70% threshold and the cost are unjustified assumptions, and the cost simply equals the invented A1 budget."}, "revision": {"status": "not_applicable", "score": null, "event_ids": [], "reason": "Revision is excluded from packet.applicable_dimensions; no scheduled update was planned or delivered."}, "recommendation": {"status": "not_reached", "score": null, "event_ids": ["A13", "A14"], "reason": "A14 records that the investigation stopped before a recommendation (context limit). A13 is an interim position only."}}, "red_flags": [{"kind": "incomplete", "event_ids": ["A14"], "reason": "The episode ended at the context limit without a completed recommendation."}, {"kind": "unsupported_inference", "event_ids": ["A13", "A9"], "reason": "A13 asserts 'growing demand for high-quality coffee in non-commercial settings' and 'historical strengths' without any source. A9 treats the A300 marketing claim as support, which uses a marketing claim as evidence of demand."}, {"kind": "unsupported_inference", "event_ids": ["A8"], "reason": "The group profile, which mentions residential kitchens, is cited as supporting a p